     Sbatch(8L)            OS-9 (News)            Sbatch(8L)     NNAAMMEE                  Sbatch  - Collect and batch News article for remote         system      SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS                  sbatch [-c|-c7|-cf|-cf7|-b|-s] [-B=<size>] [-t]                [-G=<grade>] [-f=<size>] [-C=<cmd>] [-n=<system>]                <system>     DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN                     Sbatch collects  all  article  which  should  be         send  to  a remote system.  On default all articles         are  batched  into one file until the size limit is         reached. With            --cc you  can  compress  the  news  to get a better             throughput.             --ccff forces   `freeze'   to  be  used  instead  of             compresss.             --cc77 will   encode   them   after  compression  to             transmit  them over lines which only supports 7             Bit.             --ccff77 will   be  used  for  7  Bit  channels  with             `freeze' to compress data.             --ss all articles are spooled as single files.             --ff==<<ssiizzee>> gives  the  limit  of a file in kBytes.             the default is 50 kByte.             --BB==<<bbiittccoouunntt>> To  compress  with another bitvalue             than  16  (the  default,  use the option to set             the bitvalue to 12 to 16.       Page 1                            Printed (22 Dec 1992)     Sbatch(8L)            OS-9 (News)            Sbatch(8L)           --GG==<<ggrraaddee>> If  your  delivering program accepts a             grade  character in the command string then you             can change this here.             --CC==<<ccmmdd>> the  delivery  command  can  be  changed             with   this  to  a  complete  new  value.   The             command  may  contain  two  different sequences             for  inserting  the  grade  character  and  the             system  name.   These are %%SS for the system and             %%GG for the grading.             --tt this  is for use with eight bit characters. If             your   neighbor   host  doesn't  support  these             characters  then  they  are  translated back to             pure   seven  bit  ASCII.  Currently  only  the             german umlaute for ISO8859/1 are supported.             --nn==<<ssyysstteemm>> If   the   name  in  the  command  to             forward  news  differs  from  the  filename the             batchfile  is  stored  then this is used as the             filename of the batched articles.       CCAAVVEEAATTSS                  The  files  are stored in temporary on /dd. If this         too small things may fail.       BBUUGGSS                  May be a lot, none known.       FFIILLEESS                    //hh00//SSPPOOOOLL//BBAATTCCHH The  articles  are stored herein,             for  each  system one file with the filename of             the   system.   The   format   is  an  optional             flagfield  seperated  from the main filename by             a  bar  (`||').   Currently  there  are  the two             flags  `NN'  and `CC' for non-convert and convert             from  8  bit  (if  these  optiones  are  proper             inserted the `-t' option is obsolete.)      Page 2                            Printed (22 Dec 1992)     Sbatch(8L)            OS-9 (News)            Sbatch(8L)     SSEEEE AALLSSOO                  Inews - in this distribution           Rnews - in this distribution      Page 3                            Printed (22 Dec 1992)